{
  "id": "COMPOUND:18812 - PROTEIN:5821",
  "verbalization": "Homaxisterol A2 is implicated in the biological activity of SNU-387, which is a target of multiple pathways, including one that leads to MOVP-3. The evidence suggests that Homaxisterol A2 acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn is a target of Dendocarbin K and another compound, [(1S,2S,6R,7R,9R,10S,11S,12R,14S)-11-hydroxy-14-methyl-5-methylidene-4-oxospiro[3,13-dioxatetracyclo[8.4.0.02,6.012,14]tetradecane-9,2'-oxirane]-7-yl] (E)-4-hydroxy-2-methylbut-2-enoate. This chain of targets ultimately leads to MOVP-3. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Homaxisterol A2 may influence the activity of SNU-387, which then modulates MOVP-3 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests a possible dependency on SNU-387 as a central mediator in the interaction between Homaxisterol A2 and MOVP-3, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
